   "oldText": "1. In every demonstration, locate the solid divider and measure the panels. Compare output dimensions and cell patterns against each panel (including rotations/reflections only when evidence supports them); determine whether output copies one panel, transforms it, or compares corresponding cells. Do not assume the lower or first panel is selected from orientation alone.\n2. Derive the mapping and any cross-panel rule cell by cell from demonstrations. Test every output cell, including cases where candidate inputs differ; reject any rule that misses even one location. Distinguish the candidate's exact condition (for example, a particular color pairing) from merely being in a panel, and track row/column offsets, crop, orientation, and panel dimensions explicitly. If more than one rule fits or none fits, request another demo rather than guessing.\n3. Apply only the fully verified rule to the test. Construct the exact demonstrated output dimensions and cell values; independently check each qualifying and nonqualifying position and the separator exclusion before submitting.",
   "newText": "1. Locate the solid divider in each demo and measure the panels. Compare output dimensions and cell patterns against each panel; consider rotations/reflections only when supported by evidence. Determine whether output copies/transforms one panel or compares corresponding cells. Do not select the first or lower panel from orientation alone.\n2. For a cross-panel rule, track row/column offsets, crop, orientation, and panel dimensions. Identify the exact qualifying condition (such as a color pairing), not merely panel membership; positions where candidate inputs differ are especially diagnostic.\n3. Use the shared demo-validation and submission checks in `../arc-stream-actions/SKILL.md`. In particular, exclude the separator and do not force this task family when the test lacks its defining divider."
  }
